The rule for k_recovery says it returns the object recovered from the reply, as canonical JSON text, or NO_OBJECT. For the input fence[ A ] S, the reply is a code fence containing one JSON object A followed by a sentence S. The rewritten text fence[ A ] removes the sentence S, leaving only the fence with A. The rule says the object scored is the last one inside a code fence when any fence holds one. In both texts, the fence holds A, so recovery returns A. Therefore the recovery output is unchanged between the two texts.